NAME
    addr - decode a CPU-bus address into its backing target

SYNOPSIS
    addr <addr>

DESCRIPTION
    Decodes a hex CPU-bus address through the loaded core's cartridge and
    bus mapper, reporting whether it maps to a ROM file offset, a RAM
    offset, a hardware register, or unmapped space.

    ROM offsets are reported modulo the actual ROM size, matching hardware
    mirroring. When the result maps to an addressable memory space, a
    matching 'mem' command is printed underneath for quick inspection.
    Hardware registers and unmapped addresses are reported directly
    without a synthetic offset.

EXAMPLES
    addr 808000
    addr 7E0DB3
    addr 002100

EXIT STATUS
    0   Address decoded (or usage message printed).
    1   No target attached, invalid hex address, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    mem(1), dump(1), spaces(1), vectors(1), cheat(1)
